# Motion checklist: Lasseter's principles applied to Resurgo

Source: John Lasseter, "Principles of Traditional Animation Applied to 3D Computer Animation", SIGGRAPH 1987. PDF: https://www.ics.uci.edu/~fowlkes/class/ics162/exercises/lasseter.pdf (mirror: https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/academic/class/15462-f13/www/lec_slides/Lesseter.pdf)

**Rule for every animator (Claude, Codex, Agy):** read the paper and this list before animating anything. Afterwards, report one line per principle: what you did and where.

1. **Squash and stretch.** Use subtle scale changes that preserve volume, only at moments of contact. Buttons compress to about 0.97 on press and settle back. The verdict chip lands with a single overshoot to about 1.03. Never squash text.
2. **Timing.** Duration conveys weight. Chips take 120–180 ms and windows 450–650 ms. Reading pauses scale with text length, roughly 250 ms plus 30 ms per word, so the eye can finish before the next beat. Streaming runs at about 35 characters per second. Real durations always appear as labels, even when time is compressed.
3. **Anticipation.** Cue each beat before it happens. The cursor blinks twice before typing starts. A window's title bar appears about 120 ms before its body. The spinner appears before output streams. A tab's indicator moves before its content swaps.
4. **Staging.** Run one focal action at a time. Dim inactive windows to about 0.55 opacity while another one acts. The eye path is project row, agent, terminal, clean container, verdict. Never animate the main content of two windows at once.
5. **Follow-through and overlapping action.** Children trail their parents: a window's content staggers 30–60 ms behind its frame. Lines settle with a 2 px overshoot. After the verdict lands, the tile row finishes moving a moment later.
6. **Straight-ahead versus pose-to-pose.** The story is pose-to-pose: key beats taken from the real run record (idle, failing, fixing, proving, verdict), planned first. Streaming text, timers and spinners are straight-ahead, generated as they play.
7. **Slow in and slow out.** Entrances share one easing, for example `cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)`, and exits use a gentler one. Nothing moves linearly except timers, progress and spinner rotation.
8. **Arcs.** Moving elements travel on slight curves (X and Y with different easings), not straight diagonals. The orb drifts on an arc.
9. **Exaggeration.** Push only the key moments. The failing ✗ line flashes red once for 300 ms, the winning fix line gets one quick lemon sweep, and the verdict alone gets a scale overshoot. Everything else stays calm.
10. **Secondary action.** It supports the main action and never competes with it. The orb breathes only while the model is thinking, the cursor blinks, timers tick, and tile status dots pulse softly. All of these pause when the primary action needs attention.
11. **Appeal.** Aim for clarity and personality: legible type, generous spacing, honest data and a steady rhythm. The agent should feel calm and competent, with one small flourish at the win: the lifted-r mark gives a short "lift" when a run verifies.

Also:
- `prefers-reduced-motion` shows final poses only.
- Motion is never the only signal. Every state is a word plus a glyph.
- Every replay comes from a real run record. Animation never invents a result.

## Video output quality (standing rule)
- Every video has a **4K master: 3840x2160**. Render web content at a 1920x1080 layout with deviceScaleFactor 2 so text stays crisp. Encode H.264 High at CRF 16 or better, yuv420p. Use 60 fps for motion-heavy pieces (30 fps is acceptable for slow ones).
- Platform exports come from the master, for example a high-bitrate 1080p file for X, which re-encodes uploads.
- Check the master with ffprobe (resolution, fps, codec) before calling it done.
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";
import { useReducedMotion } from "motion/react";

/** Roughly how fast agent text streams, in characters per second. */
export const CPS = 35;

/** How long the eye needs before the next beat: 250 ms plus 30 ms per word. */
export const readingMs = (text: string) => 250 + 30 * text.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;

/**
 * Stream `text` character by character, starting `delay` ms after it is set. Restarts when `text`
 * or `restartKey` changes. With reduced motion, or when `enabled` is false, the full text is shown at once.
 */
export function useStream(text: string, opts: { enabled?: boolean; restartKey?: unknown; cps?: number; delay?: number } = {}) {
  const { enabled = true, restartKey, cps = CPS, delay = 0 } = opts;
  const reduce = useReducedMotion();
  const [n, setN] = useState(0);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (reduce || !enabled) return;
    setN(0);
    const t0 = performance.now() + delay;
    const id = window.setInterval(() => {
      const k = Math.min(text.length, Math.max(0, Math.floor(((performance.now() - t0) / 1000) * cps)));
      setN(k);
      if (k >= text.length) window.clearInterval(id);
    }, 30);
    return () => window.clearInterval(id);
  }, [text, restartKey, enabled, reduce, cps, delay]);
  if (reduce || !enabled) return { shown: text, done: true, started: true };
  return { shown: text.slice(0, n), done: n >= text.length, started: n > 0 };
}

/** The last stretch of a looping cycle, when the whole story fades out before it restarts. */
const LEAVE_MS = 400;

/**
 * A playback clock in milliseconds. It runs only while the element is on screen and the tab is
 * visible, loops after `hold` ms when asked, and sits at `total` under reduced motion.
 * `live` is true while the primary beat plays; `leaving` during the fade before a loop restarts.
 */
export function useClock(total: number, opts: { loop?: boolean; hold?: number; runKey?: unknown } = {}) {
  const { loop = false, hold = 4500, runKey } = opts;
  const reduce = useReducedMotion();
  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const [t, setT] = useState(reduce ? total : 0);
  const [live, setLive] = useState(false);
  const [leaving, setLeaving] = useState(false);
  const visible = useRef(true);
  const elapsed = useRef(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    const el = ref.current;
    if (!el || typeof IntersectionObserver === "undefined") return;
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => void (visible.current = e.isIntersecting), { threshold: 0.05 });
    io.observe(el);
    return () => io.disconnect();
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    elapsed.current = 0;
    setLeaving(false);
    if (reduce) {
      setT(total);
      setLive(false);
      return;
    }
    setT(0);
    let raf = 0;
    let last = performance.now();
    const tick = (now: number) => {
      const dt = Math.min(100, now - last);
      if (now - last >= 33) {
        last = now;
        if (visible.current && !document.hidden) {
          elapsed.current += dt;
          const cycle = total + hold;
          const e = loop ? elapsed.current % cycle : Math.min(elapsed.current, total);
          setT(Math.min(e, total));
          setLive(e < total);
          setLeaving(loop && e >= cycle - LEAVE_MS);
          if (!loop && elapsed.current >= total) return;
        } else {
          setLive(false);
        }
      }
      raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    };
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    return () => {
      cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
      setLive(false);
    };
  }, [total, loop, hold, reduce, runKey]);

  return { ref, t, live, leaving, reduce: !!reduce };
}
import { useEffect, useMemo, useRef, type CSSProperties, type ReactNode } from "react";
import { Link } from "react-router-dom";
import type { RunDetail } from "@/lib/api";
import { lift, useBeatOwner } from "@/lib/beat";
import { fmtDur, shortRepo, statusMeta } from "@/lib/run";
import { frameAt, buildStory } from "@/lib/story";
import { useClock } from "@/lib/stream";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

/**
 * One window of the stack. It rises on the shared entrance easing (CSS `.win`); its title bar
 * leads and the body follows ~120 ms behind. `dim` steps it back while another window acts.
 */
function Win({
  title,
  entered,
  dim,
  children,
  className,
}: {
  title: string;
  entered: boolean;
  dim: boolean;
  children: ReactNode;
  className?: string;
}) {
  return (
    <div
      data-in={entered}
      data-dim={dim}
      className={cn(
        "win overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-terminal shadow-[0_24px_60px_-34px_color-mix(in_srgb,var(--ink)_45%,transparent)]",
        className,
      )}
    >
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-border bg-panel px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">
        <span aria-hidden className="size-2 rounded-full bg-broken" />
        <span aria-hidden className="size-2 rounded-full bg-gaps" />
        <span aria-hidden className="size-2 rounded-full bg-runs" />
        <span className="ml-2 min-w-0 flex-1 truncate">{title}</span>
      </div>
      <div className="win-body">{children}</div>
    </div>
  );
}

const stagger = (i: number, delayMs = 0) => ({ "--i": i, "--d": `${delayMs}ms` }) as CSSProperties;

/**
 * The choreographed window stack, replaying one real run: the repo card, the agent streaming its
 * recorded rationale, the terminal replaying the recorded steps, then the clean-container tiles
 * and the verdict. One window acts at a time; the others dim. Loops after a pause; under reduced
 * motion it shows the final state.
 */
export function Story({
  detail,
  loop = false,
  runKey,
  label = "Replay of a recorded run",
}: {
  detail: RunDetail;
  loop?: boolean;
  runKey?: unknown;
  label?: string;
}) {
  const story = useMemo(() => buildStory(detail), [detail]);
  const { ref, t, live, leaving, reduce } = useClock(story.total, { loop, runKey });
  const f = useMemo(() => frameAt(story, t), [story, t]);
  const s = detail.summary;
  const meta = statusMeta(s.status);
  const checking = statusMeta("checking");
  const broken = statusMeta("broken");
  const repoMeta = f.repoState === "final" ? meta : f.repoState === "broken" ? broken : checking;
  const repoWord = f.repoState === "broken" ? "Broken from a fresh clone" : repoMeta.word;
  const awaiting = s.status === "fix_awaiting_approval";
  const verified = s.verified && !awaiting; // a clean pass; an awaiting fix is not one
  const dim = (i: number) => f.focus >= 0 && f.focus !== i;

  // While this story plays its primary beat, secondary actions on the page hold still.
  useBeatOwner(live);

  // The one flourish: the lifted-r wordmark rises when a replay verifies.
  const was = useRef(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (f.verdict && !was.current && verified && !reduce) lift();
    was.current = f.verdict;
  }, [f.verdict, verified, reduce]);

  return (
    <div ref={ref} className="space-y-4" role="group" aria-label={label}>
      {/* The windows animate; this is what a screen reader gets. */}
      <p className="sr-only">
        {detail.result.repo} at {detail.result.sha}: {meta.word}
        {verified ? ", verified in a separate clean container" : awaiting ? ", the fix passed in a separate clean container and waits for the owner's approval" : ""}. {s.model_calls} model call{s.model_calls === 1 ? "" : "s"},{" "}
        {fmtDur(s.duration_s)} wall time.
      </p>
      <div aria-hidden data-leaving={leaving} className="story-group space-y-4">
        <Win title={`${detail.result.repo} @ ${detail.result.sha}`} entered={f.entered[0]} dim={dim(0)}>
          <div className="p-4">
            <div className="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <p className="text-lg font-semibold">{shortRepo(detail.result.repo)}</p>
              <span
                className={cn(
                  "chip-t inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-semibold",
                  repoMeta.tone,
                )}
              >
                <span className="font-mono">{repoMeta.glyph}</span>
                {repoWord}
              </span>
            </div>
            {f.repoState === "broken" && s.error_line && (
              <p className="settle mt-3 break-words rounded bg-evidence px-2 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-on-evidence">{s.error_line}</p>
            )}
            {f.repoState === "checking" && <p className="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Cloning fresh and running the recorded steps.</p>}
            {f.repoState === "final" && (
              <p className="settle mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                {awaiting
                  ? "The fix passed in a clean container. It changes code, so it waits for approval."
                  : story.hasFailure ? "Repaired, then re-proved in a clean container." : "Checked from a fresh clone."}
              </p>
            )}
          </div>
        </Win>

        <Win title="agent · reasoning" entered={f.entered[1]} dim={dim(1)}>
          <div className="min-h-[7.5rem] space-y-3 p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
            {f.cards.length === 0 && !f.noModelNote && <p className="text-muted-foreground">Waiting for a failure to reason about…</p>}
            {f.noModelNote && f.entered[2] && <p className="settle">{f.noModelNote}</p>}
            {f.cards.map((c) => (
              <div key={c.key} className="settle border-b border-border pb-3 last:border-b-0 last:pb-0">
                <p className="flex justify-between gap-3 text-[11px] text-muted-foreground">
                  <span className="min-w-0 truncate">{c.heading}</span>
                  <span className={cn("shrink-0 tabular-nums", c.tone === "ok" && "text-runs", c.tone === "bad" && "text-broken")}>
                    {c.right}
                  </span>
                </p>
                {c.thinking ? (
                  <p className="mt-1 text-muted-foreground">
                    <span className="mr-2">{c.spinner}</span>Thinking…
                  </p>
                ) : (
                  <p className="mt-1">
                    “{c.text}
                    {c.cursor && <span className="stream-cursor" />}
                    {!c.cursor && "”"}
                  </p>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </Win>

        <Win title={`resurgo run ${detail.result.repo}@${detail.result.sha}`} entered={f.entered[2]} dim={dim(2)}>
          <div className="flex h-[17.5rem] flex-col justify-end overflow-hidden px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-terminal-ink [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_bottom,transparent,black_1.75rem)]">
            {f.rows.map((r) => (
              <div key={r.key} className="settle shrink-0">
                <div
                  className={cn(
                    "-mx-1 flex items-baseline gap-2 rounded px-1",
                    r.flash && "flash-bad",
                    r.win && "sweep",
                  )}
                >
                  <span className="w-4 shrink-0 text-center">
                    {r.state === "done" ? (
                      <span className={r.ok ? "text-runs" : "text-broken"}>{r.kind === "think" ? "◆" : r.ok ? "✓" : "✗"}</span>
                    ) : r.state === "waiting" ? (
                      <span className="text-muted-foreground">·</span>
                    ) : (
                      <span className="text-muted-foreground">{r.spinner}</span>
                    )}
                  </span>
                  <span className="shrink-0 font-semibold">{r.label}</span>
                  {r.command !== null ? (
                    <span className="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-muted-foreground">
                      <span className="mr-1.5 text-accent-strong">$</span>
                      {r.command}
                      {r.cursor !== "none" && <span className={cn("stream-cursor", r.cursor === "blink" && "blink")} />}
                    </span>
                  ) : (
                    <span className="flex-1" />
                  )}
                  <span className="shrink-0 tabular-nums text-muted-foreground">{r.timer}</span>
                </div>
                {r.lines.map((l, i) => (
                  <div
                    key={i}
                    className={cn(
                      "settle truncate pl-6 text-xs text-muted-foreground",
                      r.ok === false || (r.ok === null && /error|ERR_|ignored build/i.test(l)) ? "text-broken" : "",
                    )}
                  >
                    {l}
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </Win>

        <Win title="clean container · rebuilt from the recipe" entered={f.entered[3]} dim={dim(3)}>
          <div className="p-4">
            {f.tiles.length === 0 ? (
              <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                {f.verdict ? "The clean container was never reached for this run." : "…"}
              </p>
            ) : (
              <ul className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-5" role="list">
                {f.tiles.map((tl, i) => (
                  <li
                    key={tl.key}
                    // After the verdict lands the tile row finishes a moment later, tile by tile.
                    style={f.verdict ? stagger(i, 120) : undefined}
                    className={cn(
                      "chip-t rounded-md border p-3",
                      f.verdict && "follow",
                      tl.state === "done" ? (tl.ok ? "border-runs/40 bg-runs-soft" : "border-broken/40 bg-broken-soft") : "border-border bg-panel",
                    )}
                  >
                    <p className="flex items-baseline gap-1.5 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold">
                      <span className={tl.state === "done" ? (tl.ok ? "text-runs" : "text-broken") : "text-muted-foreground"}>
                        {tl.state === "done" ? (tl.ok ? "✓" : "✗") : tl.state === "running" ? tl.spinner : "·"}
                      </span>
                      <span className="min-w-0 truncate">{tl.name}</span>
                    </p>
                    <p className="mt-1 h-4 font-mono text-xs tabular-nums text-muted-foreground">{tl.time}</p>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            )}
            <p
              className={cn(
                "mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-3 py-2 text-base font-semibold",
                f.verdict ? cn("verdict-land", meta.tone) : "opacity-0",
              )}
            >
              <span className="font-mono">{meta.glyph}</span>
              {meta.word}
              <span className="text-sm font-normal opacity-80">{verified ? "· verified in a separate clean container" : ""}</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </Win>
      </div>
      <p className="text-right text-sm">
        <Link to={`/runs/${s.id}`} className="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">
          Open this run
        </Link>
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
